1. Public administration in all tiers of government, including institutions and
agencies of the State, and government-controlled entities and other public
enterprises, must be governed by the democratic values and principles enshrined
in this Constitution, including the following principles--
a. a high standard of professional ethics must be promoted and maintained;
b. efficient and economical use of resources must be promoted;
c. public administration must be development-oriented;
d. services must be provided impartially, fairly, equitably and without bias;
e. people's needs must be responded to within a reasonable time, and the
public must be encouraged to participate in policy-making;
